course: dictionary
lesson: 4321
title: One word, many meanings: grow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word grow has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it. «A plant grows 2 cm a week» means it gets bigger, because the clue is the length in centimetres.
explain: Grow can also mean to plant and help things come up from the soil. «A farmer grows wheat» is about planting and caring for the crop, not about the farmer getting taller. Ask yourself: what is being grown?
explain: Grow can mean increase or become, too. «Jack's beanstalk grew up to the sky» means it got much taller. The phrase grow up, as in «Children grow up», means to change from a child into an adult. Look at the whole phrase, not just the first word.
fact: Grow means to get bigger or taller, like a child or a plant.
fact: To grow plants means to plant them and help them come up from the soil.
fact: Grow can mean to increase in number or amount, like a town or your savings.
fact: The past tense of grow is grew, and the past participle is grown: «The beanstalk grew», «The plant has grown».
fact: Grow up means to change from a child into an adult.
exercise: «A plant grows 2 cm a week.» What does grows mean here? | *Gets bigger | Falls over | Turns a different colour | Stops and sits still
exercise: «Jack's beanstalk grew up to the sky.» What does grew mean here? | *Got much taller | Fell into the river | Was painted green | Was cut down
exercise: «A farmer grows wheat.» What does grows mean here? | Counts the wheat in a bag | *Plants wheat and helps it come up from the soil | Buys wheat in a shop | Eats wheat for lunch
test: Which word is the past tense of grow? | *grew | growing | grown | grows
test: «Children grow up.» What does grow up mean? | Sing very loudly | *Change from a child into an adult | Go to bed without washing | Fall asleep early
exam: «Pollen must land on that silk or the kernel never grows.» What does grows mean here? | *Develops and gets bigger | Makes a loud noise | Falls off the cob | Shrinks and dries up
